  Verified: applied 001 → 002 → 003 in order against a scratch SQLite database; all three ran clean and the resulting
  [38;5;153musers[39m schema matches the updated [38;5;153mschema.sql[39m. Not committed.

  Two things worth knowing before this deploys:

  - [1m[38;5;153mDROP COLUMN[39m needs SQLite 3.35.0+[0m (released March 2021). I tested on 3.51.0 locally. If the production/deploy
    environment runs anything older, this migration errors out rather than silently misbehaving — worth a glance at the
    deploy job's SQLite version, since the earlier migrations would have run fine on any version.
  - [1mThe archive, if you want it.[0m You said "I think" the app no longer writes to [38;5;153mnotes[39m, and the drop is one-way. If you
    want a copy before the deploy job runs:

  sqlite3 prod.db "SELECT id, notes FROM users WHERE notes IS NOT NULL AND notes != '';" > notes_archive.tsv

    Run it against production before merge. I didn't add it to the migration — you asked for just the drop — but it's
    the difference between recoverable and not.

